# One iteration pushes until the array runs out of capacity and its elements move, and then fills the array.
# The pushes are written out one by one, because a loop that tests the length would never end with the fault injected.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeInvariantArrayStorage: the iterations of a loop are assumed to leave the storage of arrays and of typed arrays, and therefore their lengths, unchanged.
# So whatever an iteration reads of them is hoisted and read once, before the loop.
# The last two iterations read the elements at their old location. Nothing has been collected since, and nothing is stored there.
# With testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges) and with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the same operations are built in the same places.
# The hoisted values are checked against the cell inside the iteration, and the process crashes with a named error.
# AS-USERS-BUILD: under the runner's checks the code verifier rejects the injected fault at the read (walk/loops/hoisted-storage-pointer-across-a-push-is-rejected.ir). This file tests what the run-time checks catch without it.
